From 653587f6ea1dcfa629b79c889e0fdc0a66608d4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stability Audit <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] fix(tabs): persist only stable appState in canvas tabs;
 harden saveCanvasTabs

Tab snapshots embedded Excalidraw's raw appState, which can hold
non-cloneable runtime values and restored stale tool/menu state on tab switch.
- sanitizeTabAppState keeps view settings only (capture + apply, so old stored
  manifests are cleaned on restore too).
- prepareTabsForPersistence guarantees the manifest is structured-cloneable,
  degrading per tab (JSON copy, then snapshot-less shell) so one bad tab can no
  longer reject the whole manifest and lose every tab's Todo items.

Whether Excalidraw really places non-cloneable values in appState is not
confirmed in a browser. Tests: stability-tab-persistence (4). Build OK; full
suite: 76 failing = same set as baseline.
